        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4, 7, 10, 13$",
          "worked": "Shape 1 uses 4 matches. Each extra square shares a side and adds 3 matches:\nFor $x = 1$, $y = 4$.\nFor $x = 2$, $y = 4 + 3 = 7$.\nFor $x = 3$, $y = 7 + 3 = 10$.\nFor $x = 4$, $y = 10 + 3 = 13$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-flow-section-23-slot-17-slot-17-q-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Determine an equation that relates the two quantities.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y = 3x + 1$",
          "worked": "The rate of change is $m = 3$ matches per shape.\nWhen $x = 0$, $c = 4 - 3(1) = 1$.\nTherefore, the linear equation is $y = 3x + 1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-flow-section-23-slot-17-slot-17-q-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Use your equation to determine the number of matches in shape 20.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$61$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=3x+1\\\\&=3(20)+1\\\\&=61\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
